<title>CANADA: Bombardier unit to restart after spill.</title>
<headline>Bombardier unit to restart after spill.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bombardier Inc unit de Havilland Inc said it will resume business as usual on Thursday morning after halting operations on Wednesday due to a chemical spill.</p>
<p>The spill occurred mid-morning on Wednesday and has been cleared with no lingering danger to the company's workforce according to Ontario Ministry of the Environment and Ministry of Labour officials, de Havilland said.</p>
<p>De Havilland shut the facilities at 1000 EST/1500 GMT on Wednesday as a precautionary measure. Afternoon and night shifts at the Downsview, Ontario, plant were cancelled.</p>
<p>A full investigation is now under way.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
